From: Stained Glass OS contributors
Subject: user32, comctl32: push buttons and message boxes as Windows 10 draws them

Without a visual style Wine drew Windows 95's controls: bevelled grey push
buttons, a black outline round the default one, a dotted focus rectangle,
etched disabled text, and message boxes all in the face colour. Programs
that expect Windows 10's look -- installers, our own Setup -- looked old
beside everything else (field report 2: Setup's Next button, an installer's
delete-partition message box).

Push buttons are now flat: a light face and a one-pixel border; the default
or focused button's border is the highlight colour (two pixels), the one
under the pointer tinted with it (comctl32 6), a pressed one filled with it;
no dotted rectangle; disabled text in plain grey. A message box has its
message on the window colour and its buttons on a strip of the face colour.

Gate: test/flatbuttons-gate.sh (make test-flatbuttons).
---
